        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Ukrainians mark end of WWII amid fragile ceasefire with Russia Europe Issued on: 09/05/2026 - 18:19 Modified: 09/05/2026 - 18:26 As a temporary ceasefire between Ukraine and Russia comes into effect, residents across Ukraine reflect on the enduring toll of war and the uncertainty of peace. In Zaporizhzhia, mourners at a World War II memorial drew parallels between past and present suffering, while others in Kharkiv and Kyiv expressed cautious hope mixed with deep scepticism that the brief pause in fighting could lead to meaningful negotiations. Contact tracing begins after Hantavirus-hit cruise passengers disembarks in St. Helena 09/05/2026 Europe Moscow marks Victory Day amid tight security 09/05/2026 Europe 'Atmosphere closer to wartime': Moscow’s muted Victory Day reflects growing security fears 09/05/2026 Europe 'Clean break' with Orban: Hungary's Magyar to usher in 'new era' 09/05/2026 Europe Magyar to succeed Orban as Hungary's new prime minister 09/05/2026 Europe Hungary’s Magyar set to be sworn in as new prime minister 09/05/2026 Europe Hantavirus-hit cruise ship heads for Canary Islands to evacuate passengers 09/05/2026 Europe Russia marks Victory Day with scaled-back parade 09/05/2026 Europe UK: The end of the traditional two-party system? Starmer faces crushing defeat in local polls 08/05/2026 Europe"
